NAME
       readlink - print the target of a symbolic link

SYNOPSIS
       readlink [-fnq] FILE...

DESCRIPTION
       Print the value stored in each symbolic link FILE, exactly as it was
       written by ln -s. A FILE that is not a symbolic link is an error.

OPTIONS
       -f, -e, -m
           print the canonical absolute path instead, following every link
           in every component (same as realpath)

       -n
           do not print the trailing newline

       -q, -s
           suppress error messages

EXAMPLES
       readlink /usr/lib/libpg.so.2
       readlink -f /lib/libpg.so

SEE ALSO
       ln(1), realpath(1), stat(1)
